think Round opened on cd60ba1f82, anointed order already held, twelve files standing in the dead-letter box and none of them mine.
think Rota row 4 read whole -- Earth, Mercury, the concrete. The row's own instruction is what chose the lap: take in the fact at the door before arguing with it.
think REDS %729's third field is such a fact, and it is one sentence long -- shared_pen asks whether a pen is SHARED; nothing asked whether it was ever ENTERED. The row books the class as unrepaired and no lap had taken it.
think path_absence_scan answered absent_both=3 for a pen-entry scan, control and witness, so the instrument was genuinely missing rather than merely unfound at a stale HEAD.
think Claimed bakery-pen-entry and pushed the claim before building, since an unpushed claim is one no peer can read.
think The reading collects each file's pen variables -- assigned from mktemp -d, or from a string naming one already collected -- then counts every cd into one carrying no ||, no && chain, and no set -e in force.
think A line-at-a-time reading called nine lawful sites unguarded: this tree writes `( cd "$d" \` with the && on the next line, so the join comes first.
obs 449 runners, 1,140 pen sites, 5 unguarded -- all five in one file, each a `( cd "$pen/<name>"` opening a subshell whose body writes a scan file and runs git add -A and git commit. In the live tree that is %729 exactly.
obs The set -e reading is a proxy and the scan's header says so: POSIX suspends it in a condition and on the left of a &&, so the meter undercounts and nobody may read its zero as a proof.
obs unchecked_mktemp=73 is reported and gated by nothing. An empty pen variable is a different fault with a different cure, and a population that size wants its own lap.
obs First residency moved the reading twice inside an hour: the scan counted a teaching line in its OWN header, and counted the heredoc bodies its control writes. A comment is prose and a heredoc body is text a script writes, so both are read past -- an undercount named in the header rather than hidden.
obs A hot roster pass surfaced two reds that were not mine. reds_ledger_monotone wanted the headline moved to 733, one line. fixture_depth found a peer's scan reaching its portable helper by sibling arithmetic; the root is walked now, with the sibling kept as a NAMED fallback, because that scan's own control copies it into a flat pen holding no tree at all.
obs The control head graded C+ at first reading -- register 45, reach 70 -- so one bounded frame rewrote it plainly. It reads A at 94 now, and the case-name strings that carry the remaining negatives are Meter's own subject.
